From 267f0eb70391353f3e96ce2bb8cd2dbc19445e60 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Afonso Oliveira <afonso.oliveira707@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 23:40:59 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 47/47] board: spacemit: k3: do not query the serial console
 size

The only console on this board is a serial line reached through a web
terminal, whose round trip is longer than the 100 ms efi_console waits
for the answer to its cursor-position query. The answer then arrives
after the query gave up and is read by the EFI application as key
presses: Limine takes it for a key and stops its boot-menu countdown, so
the board does not boot unattended while the console is open.

The query never succeeds in time here, so the console is 80x25 either
way. Turn it off with EFI_CONSOLE_DISABLE_ANSI.
---
 configs/k3_defconfig | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/configs/k3_defconfig b/configs/k3_defconfig
index 8bf381ea..44f1fe52 100644
--- a/configs/k3_defconfig
+++ b/configs/k3_defconfig
@@ -279,3 +279,4 @@ CONFIG_SPL_LZO=y
 CONFIG_LMB_MAX_REGIONS=32
 CONFIG_EFI_VARIABLE_FILE_STORE=y
 CONFIG_EFI_RT_VOLATILE_STORE=y
+CONFIG_EFI_CONSOLE_DISABLE_ANSI=y
